	affiliations = {STIH Laboratory, Sorbonne University, 28 Rue Serpente, Paris, 75006, France; LINFI Laboratory, Biskra University, Biskra, 07000, Algeria; Paris Cité University, 45 Rue des Saints-Pères, Paris, 75006, France; LIPAH-LR11ES14, National Engineering School of Tunis (ENIT) and Faculty of Sciences of Tunis, Campus Universitaire Tunis El-Manar, Tunis, 2092, Tunisia},
	abstract = {Metacognitive and emotional dimensions of learning remain largely decoupled in current intelligent tutoring systems, overlooking theoretical evidence of their interdependence. We propose MetaEmoTutor, a unified architecture integrating metacognitive awareness with temporal emotion modeling in fine-tuned Large Language Models. The system operationalizes this integration through three key mechanisms: (i) BiLSTM-based temporal emotion modeling capturing affective evolution across dialogue, (ii) metacognitive classification inferring learners’ planning, monitoring, and evaluation processes, and (iii) LoRA-efficient LLM adaptation guiding pedagogically aligned responses. This approach bridges a critical gap by demonstrating how cognitive and emotional scaffolding can be mutually reinforcing in adaptive educational environments. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2026.},
