	affiliations = {Beijing University Of Posts And Telecommunications, International School Of Bupt, Beijing, China; Beijing University Of Posts And Telecommunications, School Of Mathematical Sciences, Beijing, China},
	abstract = {Despite rapid advances in AI-driven education, a critical gap persists between personalized student tutoring and actionable teacher insight. We present UMath, a dual-end intelligent learning platform that closes this feedback loop through a triadic data-informed architecture grounded in undergraduate mathematics pedagogy. UMath integrates large language models with structured cognitive scaffolding via three interconnected components: a metacognitive tutoring agent that provides real-time stepwise guidance and identifies emerging misconceptions, an AI-assisted lesson planner that translates insights from student-tutor interactions into adaptive instructional strategies, and a dynamic analytics dashboard that visualizes individual and cohort-level learning trajectories for instructors. This creates a closed-loop system where data continuously flows from students to teachers and back. Evaluated across multiple instructional cycles in core mathematics courses, UMath improved students' problem-solving accuracy and reasoning coherence while substantially reducing instructors' lesson preparation time. The platform illustrates how a teacher-student-AI framework can augment teaching and learning by simultaneously supporting learner agency and instructional effectiveness. Demo is available at: https://umath.cc/ © 2026 IEEE.},
