	affiliations = {School of Artificial Intelligence, Changchun Normal University, Changchun, China},
	abstract = {This paper presents EduAssist, a cloud-edge embodied interaction scaffold for child-oriented computational thinking activities. It integrates a Raspberry Pi 4B edge node, LiDAR/ultrasonic/infrared/IMU sensing, speech interaction and bounded motion actuation. The research gap addressed is the mismatch between screen-based LLM tutoring and scripted educational robots: the former offers open semantic explanation without physical feedback, whereas the latter offers embodiment without adaptive diagnosis. EduAssist therefore uses the cloud large language model only for post-event explanation, diagnostic prompting and task reconstruction; motor execution, obstacle avoidance and command validation remain local. Under 0.2-0.5 m/s low-speed conditions, multi-sensor obstacle avoidance averages 98.0% success; at 0.8m/s it decreases to 90.0%. A component ablation shows that the LiDAR-supported perception path raises the 0.8-m/s success rate from 62.0% to 90.0%. A 50-event offline semantic replay compares local-rule prompts, stateless cloud LLM diagnosis and history-aware scaffolding. The history-aware scaffold reaches 90.7% usable prompts, while local rules respond faster (5.72 ± 0.55ms) but repeat more. The results support engineering feasibility and diagnostic logging under supervised conditions, not verified child learning gains.  © 2026 IEEE.},
