	abstract = {To address the challenges in cultivating "Complex Engineering Problem"solving skills under the 2021 Washington Accord, this paper develops an AI-enhanced experimental teaching platform. Utilizing a hybrid microservice architecture, the platform integrates three core mechanisms: (1) SSE-streamed Socratic dialogue to boost engagement; (2) adaptive learning paths via AI-based modularized experimental steps; and (3) a closed-loop learning analytics system based on a multi-dimensional dynamic scoring model. Experiments in a communication engineering course show that the platform enhances students' engineering resilience and systemic thinking, resulting in a 12.3% increase in average final grades, a 47% rise in weekly activity, and a 60% improvement in grading efficiency. This research provides a replicable technical paradigm for the digital transformation of higher engineering education. © 2026 IEEE.},
