	affiliations = {School of Sciences and Engineering, University of Nicosia, Department of Computer Science, Nicosia, CY-2417, Cyprus},
	abstract = {The rapid integration of Generative AI in education presents significant opportunities for personalized learning. However, general-purpose Large Language Models frequently function as direct answer generators, which circumvents the cognitive effort necessary for deep comprehension and risks creating cognitive dependence among students. To address this challenge, this paper presents a prototype of a Socratic Co-Pilot, developed as a no-code declarative agent within the Microsoft 365 Copilot ecosystem. Utilizing Context Injection to restrict its knowledge base to specific course materials, the agent operates under strict pedagogical constraints to guide students via inquiry rather than exposition. The system is designed to support personalized learning through adaptive scaffolding and a lower-stress interaction model. By operating within an enterprise infrastructure, the prototype remains within institutional data boundaries while lowering the barrier for educator-led AI design. This paper outlines the system architecture, the pedagogical framework, and a proposed three-arm evaluation methodology within a computer science context to validate its educational impact.  © 2026 IEEE.},
