	abstract = {With the deepening application of generative AI in education, pedagogical agents should advance beyond the level of 'knowledge delivery tools' to become 'partners for thinking development.' Students' questioning ability is a key indicator of higher-order cognition, yet classrooms often face issues such as insufficient willingness to ask questions and low question quality. Based on this, this study adopts a design research approach, leveraging generative AI and integrating multiple theories to propose a scaffolded Q&A agent design model for developing questioning abilities in primary school students. Starting from the developmental stages of students' questioning abilities, the model establishes an operational mechanism of 'ability diagnosis-scaffold matching-dialogue guidance-gradual scaffold removal(gradual fading)', clearly defining the agent's functional modules and scaffold strategy configurations. This research provides a feasible and operational design framework for the transformation of generative AI from a general-purpose Q&A tool to a pedagogical agent, and also offers a new technological pathway for cultivating students' questioning ability in the classroom.  © 2026 IEEE.},
